    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3653990/extras/84b2d06ff3a33bd352166dd1934ebdc6.poster.avif?t=1749564661\" width=800 height=450 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3653990/extras/84b2d06ff3a33bd352166dd1934ebdc6.webm?t=1749564661\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3653990/extras/84b2d06ff3a33bd352166dd1934ebdc6.mp4?t=1749564661\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Mining admirers attention!</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Infploria is your go-to timesink game because you can <strong>infinitely </strong>mine and collect ores in a procedurally generated blocks environment that changes every 10 blocks. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Additionally there is the chance of rare occurrences happening while mining. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Can you reach to the Core of the Earth to mine Coresium?</p>",
